IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgg-scope`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 11 Division 2: ss 377 to 377D -- what happens when a foreign company stops doing business in Singapore,
-- goes into liquidation or is dissolved, is struck off the register, and is restored. Part sgg, layer 1.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is the section's own test met; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words (tagged FALSE-kind);
-- NOTHING is "the text does not say" (tagged NOTHING-kind). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Provisions that address only the Registrar, the Minister or the Court are functions over the facts that decide them; there is no seat for an official.

§ `Section 377(1) to (1B): notice that the foreign company has ceased to do business in Singapore`

DECLARE `s 377 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 377(1) lodge with the Registrar notice that the foreign company has ceased to have a place of business or to carry on business in Singapore`
    `s 377(2) lodge with the Registrar notice that the foreign company has gone into liquidation or has been dissolved`
    `s 377(2) lodge with the Registrar notice of the appointment of a liquidator`

-- src:24627 | Cesser of business in Singapore
-- src:24629 | 377.—(1) If a foreign company ceases to have a place of business in
-- src:24630 | Singapore or to carry on business in Singapore, it must, within 7 days
-- src:24631 | after so ceasing, lodge with the Registrar notice of that fact.
@ref s 377(1) (src:24627-24631)
GIVEN `the foreign company has ceased to have a place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has ceased to carry on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(1) the foreign company must lodge with the Registrar notice that it has ceased` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company has ceased to have a place of business in Singapore` OR `the foreign company has ceased to carry on business in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a foreign company ceases to have a place of business in Singapore or to carry on business in Singapore, it must ... lodge with the Registrar notice of that fact" (a duty gated by "If": fork F-D1)

@ref s 377(1) (src:24629-24631)
GIVEN `the day the foreign company ceased` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice was lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(1) the notice was lodged within 7 days after the foreign company ceased` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the foreign company ceased` `the day the notice was lodged` 7 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must, within 7 days after so ceasing, lodge with the Registrar notice of that fact" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); "within 7 days after" is counted as "not later than 7 days after": fork F-P1)

@ref s 377(1) (src:24629-24631)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 377 act`
`s 377(1) the foreign company must lodge the notice within 7 days after it ceases` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 377(1) lodge with the Registrar notice that the foreign company has ceased to have a place of business or to carry on business in Singapore`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the notice that the foreign company has ceased to do business in Singapore was not lodged within 7 days after it ceased"

-- (1A) "Starting on the day on which the foreign company lodged the notice ..., the foreign company's obligation to lodge any document (not being a document that ought to have been lodged before that day) with the Registrar ceases."
-- src:24635 | (1A) Starting on the day on which the foreign company lodged the
-- src:24636 | notice mentioned in subsection (1), the foreign company’s obligation
-- src:24641 | to lodge any document (not being a document that ought to have been
-- src:24642 | lodged before that day) with the Registrar ceases.
@ref s 377(1A) (src:24635-24642)
GIVEN `the foreign company lodged the notice mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the document ought to have been lodged before the day the notice was lodged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(1A) the obligation of the foreign company to lodge the document with the Registrar has ceased` MEANS
    IF NOT `the foreign company lodged the notice mentioned in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Starting on the day on which the foreign company lodged the notice mentioned in subsection (1), the foreign company's obligation to lodge any document ... ceases" (the cessation starts with the lodging, in the text's own words: no notice, no starting day)
    ELSE (IF `the document ought to have been lodged before the day the notice was lodged`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(not being a document that ought to have been lodged before that day)": such a document is taken out of the cessation
          ELSE (IF `the day asked` LESS THAN `the day the notice was lodged`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Starting on the day on which the foreign company lodged the notice": before that day the cessation has not begun
                ELSE JUST TRUE))

-- src:24646 | (1B) The Registrar must as soon as practicable after the lodgment
-- src:24647 | of the notice mentioned in subsection (1) record in the register that the
-- src:24648 | company has ceased to have a place of business in Singapore or
-- src:24649 | ceased to carry on business in Singapore, as the case may be.
@ref s 377(1B) (src:24646-24649)
GIVEN `the foreign company lodged the notice mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has ceased to have a place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(1B) the Registrar must record in the register that the company has ceased to have a place of business in Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company lodged the notice mentioned in subsection (1)` AND `the foreign company has ceased to have a place of business in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must as soon as practicable after the lodgment of the notice mentioned in subsection (1) record in the register that the company has ceased to have a place of business in Singapore ..., as the case may be" (a duty that arises on the lodgment and the case that applies: fork F-D1)

@ref s 377(1B) (src:24646-24649)
GIVEN `the foreign company lodged the notice mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has ceased to carry on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(1B) the Registrar must record in the register that the company has ceased to carry on business in Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company lodged the notice mentioned in subsection (1)` AND `the foreign company has ceased to carry on business in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "record in the register that the company has ... ceased to carry on business in Singapore, as the case may be" (a duty that arises on the lodgment and the case that applies: fork F-D1)

§ `Section 377(2): liquidation or dissolution of the foreign company`

-- (2) "each person who immediately before the commencement of the liquidation proceedings was an authorised representative must (a) within 14 days after the commencement of the liquidation or the dissolution; or
-- (b) within such further time as the Registrar in special circumstances allows, lodge or cause to be lodged with the Registrar notice of that fact and, when a liquidator is appointed, notice of such appointment."
-- src:24653 | (2) If a foreign company goes into liquidation or is dissolved in its
-- src:24654 | place of incorporation or origin, each person who immediately before
-- src:24655 | the commencement of the liquidation proceedings was an authorised
-- src:24656 | representative must —
-- src:24658 | (a) within 14 days after the commencement of the liquidation
-- src:24659 | or the dissolution; or
-- src:24661 | (b) within such further time as the Registrar in special
-- src:24662 | circumstances allows,
-- src:24664 | lodge or cause to be lodged with the Registrar notice of that fact and,
-- src:24665 | when a liquidator is appointed, notice of such appointment.
@ref s 377(2) (src:24653-24665)
GIVEN `the foreign company has gone into liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has been dissolved in its place of incorporation or origin` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was an authorised representative immediately before the commencement of the liquidation proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(2) the person must lodge or cause to be lodged with the Registrar notice of the liquidation or the dissolution` MEANS
    IF (`the foreign company has gone into liquidation` OR `the foreign company has been dissolved in its place of incorporation or origin`) AND `the person was an authorised representative immediately before the commencement of the liquidation proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a foreign company goes into liquidation or is dissolved in its place of incorporation or origin, each person who immediately before the commencement of the liquidation proceedings was an authorised representative must ... lodge" (a duty gated by "If": fork F-D1)

@ref s 377(2) (src:24658-24662)
GIVEN `the day the liquidation or the dissolution commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar in special circumstances allowed further time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the further time the Registrar allowed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(2) the notice was lodged within the time the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the liquidation or the dissolution commenced` `the day the notice was lodged` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (IF `the Registrar in special circumstances allowed further time` AND `the day the notice was lodged` AT MOST `the last day of the further time the Registrar allowed`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) within 14 days after the commencement of the liquidation or the dissolution; or (b) within such further time as the Registrar in special circumstances allows" (the two limbs are the whole of the time the subsection gives; "within 14 days after" is counted as "not later than 14 days after": fork F-P1; the further time is taken as ending on the last day the Registrar allowed, whether it is added to the 14 days or replaces them: fork F-T1)

-- The rule for limb (a): the party is each authorised representative, the act is the lodgment, the time limit is 14 days from the commencement of the liquidation or the dissolution (the trace starts on that day).
@ref s 377(2)(a) (src:24658-24659)
GIVEN `the name of the authorised representative` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 377 act`
`s 377(2)(a) an authorised representative must lodge notice of the liquidation or the dissolution within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` `the name of the authorised representative`
    MUST `s 377(2) lodge with the Registrar notice that the foreign company has gone into liquidation or has been dissolved`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` `the name of the authorised representative` BECAUSE "the notice of the liquidation or the dissolution was not lodged within 14 days after its commencement"

-- Limb (b): the further time is whatever the Registrar in special circumstances allows, so the day count is an input, counted from the same starting day.
@ref s 377(2)(b) (src:24661-24662)
GIVEN `the name of the authorised representative` IS A STRING
      `the last day the Registrar in special circumstances allows, counted in days from the commencement of the liquidation or the dissolution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 377 act`
`s 377(2)(b) an authorised representative must lodge notice of the liquidation or the dissolution within the further time the Registrar allows` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` `the name of the authorised representative`
    MUST `s 377(2) lodge with the Registrar notice that the foreign company has gone into liquidation or has been dissolved`
    WITHIN `the last day the Registrar in special circumstances allows, counted in days from the commencement of the liquidation or the dissolution`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` `the name of the authorised representative` BECAUSE "the notice of the liquidation or the dissolution was not lodged within the further time the Registrar allowed"

-- "and, when a liquidator is appointed, notice of such appointment": read as not governed by the 14 days in (a) or the further time in (b) (assumed, not ruled; fork F-T2), so the s 52 input sets the time (notes/lest-without-deadline.md).
@ref s 377(2) (src:24664-24665)
GIVEN `the foreign company has gone into liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a liquidator has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was an authorised representative immediately before the commencement of the liquidation proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(2) the person must lodge or cause to be lodged with the Registrar notice of the appointment of a liquidator` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company has gone into liquidation` AND `a liquidator has been appointed` AND `the person was an authorised representative immediately before the commencement of the liquidation proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "each person who immediately before the commencement of the liquidation proceedings was an authorised representative must ... lodge or cause to be lodged with the Registrar ... when a liquidator is appointed, notice of such appointment" (a duty gated by "when": fork F-D1)

@ref s 377(2) (src:24664-24665)
GIVEN `the name of the authorised representative` IS A STRING
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 377 act`
`s 377(2) an authorised representative must lodge notice of the appointment of a liquidator when one is appointed` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` `the name of the authorised representative`
    MUST `s 377(2) lodge with the Registrar notice of the appointment of a liquidator`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` `the name of the authorised representative` BECAUSE "the notice of the appointment of a liquidator was not lodged"

§ `Section 377(5) to (13): the Registrar records a dissolution, strikes off the name, and the appeal`

-- src:24675 | (5) On receipt of a notice from an authorised representative that the
-- src:24676 | foreign company has been dissolved, the Registrar must record in the
-- src:24677 | register that the foreign company has been dissolved.
@ref s 377(5) (src:24675-24677)
GIVEN `the Registrar has received a notice from an authorised representative that the foreign company has been dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(5) the Registrar must record in the register that the foreign company has been dissolved` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has received a notice from an authorised representative that the foreign company has been dissolved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On receipt of a notice from an authorised representative that the foreign company has been dissolved, the Registrar must record in the register that the foreign company has been dissolved" (a duty gated by "On receipt": fork F-D1)

-- (8) "must strike the name of a foreign company off the register if the Registrar is satisfied that the company is being used for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore or against the national security or interest."
-- src:24685 | (8) The Registrar must strike the name of a foreign company off the
-- src:24686 | register if the Registrar is satisfied that the company is being used for
-- src:24687 | an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace,
-- src:24688 | welfare or good order in Singapore or against the national security or
-- src:24689 | interest.
@ref s 377(8) (src:24685-24689)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the company is being used for an unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the company is being used for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the company is being used against the national security or interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(8) the Registrar must strike the name of the foreign company off the register` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is satisfied that the company is being used for an unlawful purpose` OR `the Registrar is satisfied that the company is being used for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore` OR `the Registrar is satisfied that the company is being used against the national security or interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must strike the name of a foreign company off the register if the Registrar is satisfied that ..." (a duty gated by "if": fork F-D1)

-- (9)(b) "the company has failed to appoint an authorised representative within 6 months after the date of the death of its sole authorised representative".
-- src:24696 | (9) The Registrar may strike the name of a foreign company off the
-- src:24697 | register if —
-- src:24699 | (a) the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the
-- src:24700 | company has ceased to carry on business or to have a place
-- src:24701 | of business in Singapore; or
-- src:24703 | (b) the company has failed to appoint an authorised
-- src:24704 | representative within 6 months after the date of the death
-- src:24705 | of its sole authorised representative.
@ref s 377(9) (src:24696-24705)
GIVEN `the day the sole authorised representative died` IS A DATE
      `the company appointed an authorised representative within 6 months after the date of the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(9)(b) the company has failed to appoint an authorised representative within 6 months after the death of its sole authorised representative` MEANS
    IF `the company appointed an authorised representative within 6 months after the date of the death`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company has failed to appoint an authorised representative within 6 months after the date of the death": one appointed in the 6 months is no failure
    ELSE (IF `the day asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the sole authorised representative died` 6 Months
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 6 months after the date of the death": before the 6 months have run out there is no failure yet (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a))

@ref s 377(9) (src:24696-24705)
GIVEN `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the company has ceased to carry on business or to have a place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has failed to appoint an authorised representative within 6 months after the date of the death of its sole authorised representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(9) the Registrar may strike the name of the foreign company off the register` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the company has ceased to carry on business or to have a place of business in Singapore` OR `the company has failed to appoint an authorised representative within 6 months after the date of the death of its sole authorised representative`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registrar may strike the name of a foreign company off the register if (a) ...; or (b) ..." names two grounds without "only if", so the subsection does not say the Registrar may not strike off on another ground (grant rule 2026-11-12; marginal reading (b))

-- (10)(a) "the sole authorised representative has given written notice to the foreign company that he or she desires to resign and has lodged a notice under section 370(3) with the Registrar,
-- but the company has failed to respond or appoint another authorised representative within 12 months after the date of lodgment of the notice".
-- src:24709 | (10) The Registrar may strike the name of a foreign company off
-- src:24710 | the register upon the application of the sole authorised representative
-- src:24711 | of the foreign company in the prescribed form if the Registrar is
-- src:24712 | satisfied that —
-- src:24714 | (a) the sole authorised representative has given written notice
-- src:24715 | to the foreign company that he or she desires to resign and
-- src:24716 | has lodged a notice under section 370(3) with the Registrar,
-- src:24717 | but the company has failed to respond or appoint another
-- src:24718 | authorised representative within 12 months after the date
-- src:24719 | of lodgment of the notice; or
-- src:24721 | (b) the foreign company has failed to give instructions with
-- src:24722 | respect to a written request from the sole authorised
-- src:24723 | representative for instructions as to whether the company
-- src:24724 | wishes to cancel or continue its registration under this Act
-- src:24725 | within 12 months after the date the written request was
-- src:24726 | sent.
@ref s 377(10) (src:24709-24726)
GIVEN `the sole authorised representative has given written notice to the foreign company that he or she desires to resign` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sole authorised representative has lodged a notice under section 370(3) with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice under section 370(3) was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the company responded or appointed another authorised representative within 12 months after the date of lodgment of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(10)(a) the company has failed to respond or appoint another authorised representative within 12 months after the date of lodgment of the notice` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the sole authorised representative has given written notice to the foreign company that he or she desires to resign` AND `the sole authorised representative has lodged a notice under section 370(3) with the Registrar`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the sole authorised representative has given written notice ... and has lodged a notice under section 370(3) with the Registrar, but the company has failed ..." (the paragraph's own first elements unmet)
    ELSE (IF `the company responded or appointed another authorised representative within 12 months after the date of lodgment of the notice`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but the company has failed to respond or appoint another authorised representative within 12 months": a response or an appointment in the 12 months is no failure
          ELSE (IF `the day asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the notice under section 370(3) was lodged` 12 Months
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 12 months after the date of lodgment of the notice": before the 12 months have run out there is no failure yet (periods ruling item (a))

@ref s 377(10)(b) (src:24721-24726)
GIVEN `the sole authorised representative sent the foreign company a written request for instructions as to whether the company wishes to cancel or continue its registration under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the written request was sent` IS A DATE
      `the foreign company gave instructions within 12 months after the date the written request was sent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(10)(b) the foreign company has failed to give instructions within 12 months after the date the written request was sent` MEANS
    IF NOT `the sole authorised representative sent the foreign company a written request for instructions as to whether the company wishes to cancel or continue its registration under this Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the foreign company has failed to give instructions with respect to a written request from the sole authorised representative for instructions as to whether the company wishes to cancel or continue its registration under this Act": with no such request there is nothing to fail
    ELSE (IF `the foreign company gave instructions within 12 months after the date the written request was sent`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has failed to give instructions ... within 12 months": instructions in the 12 months are no failure
          ELSE (IF `the day asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the written request was sent` 12 Months
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 12 months after the date the written request was sent": before the 12 months have run out there is no failure yet (periods ruling item (a))

-- (10) "The Registrar may strike the name of a foreign company off the register upon the application of the sole authorised representative of the foreign company in the prescribed form if the Registrar is satisfied that (a) ...; or (b) ...".
-- A "may" gated by "upon the application": split site (ii); the answer taken is JUST FALSE when there is no application (fork F-S3); the "if the Registrar is satisfied" gate is NOTHING when it fails (grant rule).
@ref s 377(10) (src:24709-24726)
GIVEN `the sole authorised representative applied in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that paragraph (a) is made out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that paragraph (b) is made out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(10) the Registrar may strike the name of the foreign company off the register on the application of the sole authorised representative` MEANS
    IF NOT `the sole authorised representative applied in the prescribed form`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar may strike the name of a foreign company off the register upon the application of the sole authorised representative of the foreign company in the prescribed form" (a "may" gated by "upon the application": split site (ii), answer JUST FALSE: fork F-S3)
    ELSE (IF `the Registrar is satisfied that paragraph (a) is made out` OR `the Registrar is satisfied that paragraph (b) is made out`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Registrar is satisfied that (a) ...; or (b) ..." names two grounds without "only if" (grant rule 2026-11-12; marginal reading (b))

-- (11) "Without limiting subsection (9)(a), in determining whether there is reasonable ground to believe that a company is not carrying on business under that subsection, the Registrar may have regard to such circumstances as may be prescribed."
-- src:24730 | (11) Without limiting subsection (9)(a), in determining whether
-- src:24731 | there is reasonable ground to believe that a company is not carrying
-- src:24732 | on business under that subsection, the Registrar may have regard to
-- src:24733 | such circumstances as may be prescribed.
@ref s 377(11) (src:24730-24733)
GIVEN `the determination is a determination under subsection (9)(a) whether there is reasonable ground to believe that a company is not carrying on business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(11) the Registrar may have regard to the circumstances prescribed` MEANS
    IF `the determination is a determination under subsection (9)(a) whether there is reasonable ground to believe that a company is not carrying on business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in determining whether there is reasonable ground to believe that a company is not carrying on business under that subsection, the Registrar may have regard to such circumstances as may be prescribed" speaks of that determination only; the circumstances prescribed are not in the sources

-- (12) "For the purposes of subsections (9) and (10), the provisions of this Act relating to the striking off the register of the name of a defunct company extend and apply with such adaptations as are necessary."
-- src:24737 | (12) For the purposes of subsections (9) and (10), the provisions of
-- src:24738 | this Act relating to the striking off the register of the name of a
-- src:24739 | defunct company extend and apply with such adaptations as are
-- src:24740 | necessary.
@ref s 377(12) (src:24737-24740)
GIVEN `the striking off is a striking off under subsection (9) or (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(12) the provisions of this Act relating to the striking off of a defunct company apply with the adaptations necessary` MEANS
    IF `the striking off is a striking off under subsection (9) or (10)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the provisions on striking off a defunct company, and which adaptations are necessary, are not in this part's ranges; the subsection reaches only strikings off under (9) or (10)

-- (13) "Any person aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under subsection (8), (9) or (10) may, within 30 days after the date of the decision, appeal to the Minister whose decision is final."
-- src:24747 | (13) Any person aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under
-- src:24748 | subsection (8), (9) or (10) may, within 30 days after the date of the
-- src:24749 | decision, appeal to the Minister whose decision is final.
@ref s 377(13) (src:24747-24749)
GIVEN `the person is aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is a decision under subsection (8), (9) or (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE
      `the day the appeal to the Minister is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(13) the person may appeal to the Minister` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar` AND `the decision is a decision under subsection (8), (9) or (10)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under subsection (8), (9) or (10)" names who may appeal and from which decisions, without "only"
    ELSE (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the decision` `the day the appeal to the Minister is made` 30 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, within 30 days after the date of the decision, appeal to the Minister" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); "within 30 days after" is counted as "not later than 30 days after": fork F-P1)

@ref s 377(13) (src:24747-24749)
GIVEN `the appeal is an appeal under subsection (13)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(13) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is an appeal under subsection (13)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "appeal to the Minister whose decision is final" speaks only of an appeal under this subsection

§ `Section 377A: application for administrative restoration`

-- (1) "Subject to such conditions as may be prescribed, a director or member of a foreign company whose name has been struck off the register under section 377(9) or (10) may apply to the Registrar to restore the name of the company to the register."
-- src:24753 | Application for administrative restoration of foreign company
-- src:24754 | to register
-- src:24756 | 377A.—(1) Subject to such conditions as may be prescribed, a
-- src:24757 | director or member of a foreign company whose name has been
-- src:24758 | struck off the register under section 377(9) or (10) may apply to the
-- src:24759 | Registrar to restore the name of the company to the register.
@ref s 377A(1) (src:24753-24759)
GIVEN `the person is a director or member of the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name of the foreign company has been struck off the register under section 377(9) or (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377A(1) the person may apply to the Registrar to restore the name of the foreign company to the register` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director or member of the foreign company` AND `the name of the foreign company has been struck off the register under section 377(9) or (10)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a director or member of a foreign company whose name has been struck off the register under section 377(9) or (10) may apply" names who may apply and for which companies, without "only"; the conditions prescribed are not in the sources

-- (2) "An application under this section is not valid unless the application is received by the Registrar within 6 years after the date on which the name of the foreign company is struck off the register." A bar, answered in the bar's direction.
-- src:24763 | (2) An application under this section is not valid unless the
-- src:24764 | application is received by the Registrar within 6 years after the
-- src:24765 | date on which the name of the foreign company is struck off the
-- src:24766 | register.
@ref s 377A(2) (src:24763-24766)
GIVEN `the day the name of the foreign company was struck off the register` IS A DATE
      `the day the application was received by the Registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377A(2) the application is not valid` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the name of the foreign company was struck off the register` `the day the application was received by the Registrar` 6 Years
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is not valid unless the application is received by the Registrar within 6 years": once received in time the bar lifts, and the subsection does not say the application is valid
    ELSE JUST TRUE   -- the bar applies: "is not valid unless ..." (a flat negative with "unless"; "within 6 years after" is counted as "not later than 6 years after": fork F-P1)

§ `Section 377B: the Registrar's decision on an application for administrative restoration`

-- src:24770 | Registrar’s decision on application for administrative
-- src:24771 | restoration of foreign company
-- src:24773 | 377B.—(1) The Registrar must give notice to the applicant of the
-- src:24774 | decision on an application under section 377A.
@ref s 377B(1) (src:24770-24774)
GIVEN `the application is an application under section 377A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377B(1) the Registrar must give notice to the applicant of the decision` MEANS
    IF `the application is an application under section 377A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must give notice to the applicant of the decision on an application under section 377A" (a duty on one kind of application: fork F-D1)

-- src:24778 | (2) If the Registrar’s decision is that the name of the foreign
-- src:24779 | company should be restored to the register, the name of the company
-- src:24780 | is restored to the register on the date on which notice is sent (called in
-- src:24781 | this section the restoration date).
@ref s 377B(2) (src:24778-24781)
GIVEN `the Registrar's decision is that the name of the foreign company should be restored to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice is sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 377B(2) the restoration date` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar's decision is that the name of the foreign company should be restored to the register`
    THEN JUST `the day the notice is sent`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Registrar's decision is that the name of the foreign company should be restored to the register, the name of the company is restored ... on the date on which notice is sent": with another decision the subsection names no restoration date

-- src:24785 | (3) The Registrar must —
-- src:24787 | (a) enter in the register a note of the restoration date; and
-- src:24789 | (b) cause notice of the restoration to be published in the
-- src:24790 | Gazette and on the Authority’s website.
@ref s 377B(3) (src:24785-24790)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company has been restored under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377B(3)(a) the Registrar must enter in the register a note of the restoration date` MEANS
    IF `the name of the foreign company has been restored under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must — (a) enter in the register a note of the restoration date": the restoration date exists only on a decision to restore, so the duty is read as gated by it (fork F-D1)

@ref s 377B(3) (src:24789-24790)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company has been restored under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377B(3)(b) the Registrar must cause notice of the restoration to be published in the Gazette and on the Authority's website` MEANS
    IF `the name of the foreign company has been restored under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must — ... (b) cause notice of the restoration to be published in the Gazette and on the Authority's website": the notice is a notice of a restoration, so the duty is read as gated by one (fork F-D1)

-- (4) "The notice under subsection (3)(b) must state — (a) the name of the foreign company or, if the company is restored to the register under a different name, that name and its former name;
-- (b) the unique entity number of the foreign company issued by the Registrar; and (c) the restoration date."
-- src:24794 | (4) The notice under subsection (3)(b) must state —
-- src:24796 | (a) the name of the foreign company or, if the company is
-- src:24797 | restored to the register under a different name, that name
-- src:24798 | and its former name;
-- src:24803 | (b) the unique entity number of the foreign company issued by
-- src:24804 | the Registrar; and
-- src:24806 | (c) the restoration date.
@ref s 377B(4) (src:24794-24806)
GIVEN `the company is restored to the register under a different name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the name of the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the former name of the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the unique entity number of the foreign company issued by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the restoration date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377B(4) the notice states everything the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice states the name of the foreign company` AND ((NOT `the company is restored to the register under a different name`) OR `the notice states the former name of the foreign company`) AND `the notice states the unique entity number of the foreign company issued by the Registrar` AND `the notice states the restoration date`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice under subsection (3)(b) must state — (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..." (a duty whose content is not met)

-- src:24810 | (5) If the Registrar’s decision is that the name of the foreign
-- src:24811 | company should not be restored to the register, the person who made
-- src:24812 | the application under section 377A or any other person aggrieved by
-- src:24813 | the decision of the Registrar, may appeal to the Court.
@ref s 377B(5) (src:24810-24813)
GIVEN `the Registrar's decision is that the name of the foreign company should not be restored to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made the application under section 377A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is any other person aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377B(5) the person may appeal to the Court` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar's decision is that the name of the foreign company should not be restored to the register` AND (`the person made the application under section 377A` OR `the person is any other person aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Registrar's decision is that the name of the foreign company should not be restored ..., the person who made the application ... or any other person aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar, may appeal to the Court" names the decision and the persons, without "only"

-- src:24817 | (6) On an appeal made under subsection (5), the Court may —
-- src:24819 | (a) confirm the Registrar’s decision; or
-- src:24821 | (b) restore the name of the foreign company to the register and
-- src:24822 | give such directions and make such orders as the Court is
-- src:24823 | empowered to give and make under section 377D(3).
@ref s 377B(6) (src:24817-24823)
GIVEN `the appeal is an appeal made under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377B(6)(a) the Court may confirm the Registrar's decision` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is an appeal made under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On an appeal made under subsection (5), the Court may — (a) confirm the Registrar's decision" speaks of that appeal only

@ref s 377B(6) (src:24821-24823)
GIVEN `the appeal is an appeal made under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377B(6)(b) the Court may restore the name of the foreign company to the register and give the directions and make the orders that section 377D(3) allows` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is an appeal made under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On an appeal made under subsection (5), the Court may — ... (b) restore the name of the foreign company to the register and give such directions and make such orders as the Court is empowered to give and make under section 377D(3)" speaks of that appeal only

§ `Section 377C: the Registrar restores a foreign company deregistered by mistake`

-- (2) "In subsection (1), a reference to a mistake of the Registrar excludes a mistake that is made on the basis of wrong, false or misleading information given by an applicant in connection with an application for striking the name of the foreign company off the register under section 377(10)."
-- src:24827 | Registrar may restore foreign company deregistered by
-- src:24828 | mistake
-- src:24830 | 377C.—(1) The Registrar may, on his or her own initiative, restore
-- src:24831 | the name of a foreign company to the register if the Registrar is
-- src:24832 | satisfied that the name of the company has been struck off the register
-- src:24833 | under section 377(9) or (10) as a result of a mistake of the Registrar.
-- src:24837 | (2) In subsection (1), a reference to a mistake of the Registrar
-- src:24838 | excludes a mistake that is made on the basis of wrong, false or
-- src:24839 | misleading information given by an applicant in connection with an
-- src:24840 | application for striking the name of the foreign company off the
-- src:24841 | register under section 377(10).
@ref s 377C(1) (src:24827-24841)
GIVEN `the mistake was made on the basis of wrong, false or misleading information given by an applicant in connection with an application for striking the name of the foreign company off the register under section 377(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(2) the mistake is a mistake of the Registrar within subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the mistake was made on the basis of wrong, false or misleading information given by an applicant in connection with an application for striking the name of the foreign company off the register under section 377(10)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference to a mistake of the Registrar excludes a mistake that is made on the basis of wrong, false or misleading information given by an applicant in connection with an application for striking the name ... off the register under section 377(10)"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection excludes one kind of mistake and does not say what else is a mistake of the Registrar

@ref s 377C(1) (src:24830-24833)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the name of the company has been struck off the register under section 377(9) or (10) as a result of a mistake of the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(1) the Registrar may on his or her own initiative restore the name of the foreign company to the register` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is satisfied that the name of the company has been struck off the register under section 377(9) or (10) as a result of a mistake of the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registrar may, on his or her own initiative, restore the name of a foreign company to the register if the Registrar is satisfied that ..." names one ground without "only if" (grant rule 2026-11-12; marginal reading (b))

-- (3) "The Registrar may restore the name of a foreign company to the register by publishing in the Gazette and on the Authority's website a notice declaring the restoration, and the restoration takes effect on the date of publication of the notice."
-- src:24845 | (3) The Registrar may restore the name of a foreign company to the
-- src:24846 | register by publishing in the Gazette and on the Authority’s website a
-- src:24847 | notice declaring the restoration, and the restoration takes effect on the
-- src:24848 | date of publication of the notice.
@ref s 377C(3) (src:24845-24848)
GIVEN `the Registrar has published in the Gazette a notice declaring the restoration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has published on the Authority's website a notice declaring the restoration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377C(3) the Registrar may restore the name of the foreign company by publishing the notice` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has published in the Gazette a notice declaring the restoration` AND `the Registrar has published on the Authority's website a notice declaring the restoration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registrar may restore the name ... by publishing in the Gazette and on the Authority's website a notice declaring the restoration" names the way the power is used, without "only"

@ref s 377C(3) (src:24847-24848)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company is restored by publication of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice is published` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 377C(3) the day the restoration takes effect` MEANS
    IF `the name of the foreign company is restored by publication of the notice`
    THEN JUST `the day the notice is published`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the restoration takes effect on the date of publication of the notice" speaks of a restoration by that notice

§ `Section 377D: the effect of restoration`

-- src:24855 | Effect of restoration of foreign company
-- src:24857 | 377D.—(1) If the name of a foreign company is restored to the
-- src:24858 | register under section 377B(2) or 377C, or on appeal to the Court
-- src:24859 | under section 377B(5), the company is to be regarded as having
-- src:24860 | continued its registration under this Act as if the name of the company
-- src:24861 | had not been struck off the register.
@ref s 377D(1) (src:24855-24861)
GIVEN `the name was restored under section 377B(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name was restored under section 377C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name was restored on appeal to the Court under section 377B(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377D(1) the foreign company is regarded as having continued its registration as if its name had not been struck off the register` MEANS
    IF `the name was restored under section 377B(2)` OR `the name was restored under section 377C` OR `the name was restored on appeal to the Court under section 377B(5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the name of a foreign company is restored to the register under section 377B(2) or 377C, or on appeal to the Court under section 377B(5), the company is to be regarded as having continued its registration" (a deeming gated by "If": periods ruling item (b); marginal reading (a))

-- (2) "The foreign company, its directors or equivalent persons, and authorised representatives are not liable to a penalty under section 373(18) for a financial year in relation to which the period for filing ... ended (a) after the date on which the name of the company was struck off the register; and (b) before the restoration of the name".
-- src:24865 | (2) The foreign company, its directors or equivalent persons, and
-- src:24866 | authorised representatives are not liable to a penalty under
-- src:24867 | section 373(18) for a financial year in relation to which the period
-- src:24868 | for filing its balance sheet, cash flow statement, profit and loss
-- src:24869 | statement and other related documents ended —
-- src:24871 | (a) after the date on which the name of the company was
-- src:24872 | struck off the register; and
-- src:24874 | (b) before the restoration of the name of the company to the
-- src:24875 | register.
@ref s 377D(2) (src:24865-24875)
GIVEN `the role of the person` IS A `s 365 role`
      `the day the name of the company was struck off the register` IS A DATE
      `the day the period for filing the balance sheet, cash flow statement, profit and loss statement and other related documents for the financial year ended` IS A DATE
      `the day the name of the company was restored to the register` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377D(2) the person is not liable to a penalty under section 373(18) for the financial year` MEANS
    IF NOT (   `the role of the person` EQUALS `s 365 role: the foreign company`
            OR `the role of the person` EQUALS `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person`
            OR `the role of the person` EQUALS `s 365 role: an authorised representative of the foreign company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The foreign company, its directors or equivalent persons, and authorised representatives are not liable" names who is relieved, without "only"
    ELSE (IF `the day the name of the company was struck off the register` LESS THAN `the day the period for filing the balance sheet, cash flow statement, profit and loss statement and other related documents for the financial year ended` AND `the day the period for filing the balance sheet, cash flow statement, profit and loss statement and other related documents for the financial year ended` LESS THAN `the day the name of the company was restored to the register`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for a financial year in relation to which the period for filing ... ended (a) after the date on which the name of the company was struck off the register; and (b) before the restoration" names the years it relieves, without "only"

-- (3) "On the application by any person, the Court may give directions and make orders, as seem just for placing the foreign company and all other persons in the same position (as nearly as may be) as if the name of the company had not been struck off the register."
-- src:24879 | (3) On the application by any person, the Court may give directions
-- src:24880 | and make orders, as seem just for placing the foreign company and all
-- src:24881 | other persons in the same position (as nearly as may be) as if the name
-- src:24882 | of the company had not been struck off the register.
@ref s 377D(3) (src:24879-24882)
GIVEN `a person has applied to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377D(3) the Court may give directions and make orders as seem just for placing the foreign company and all other persons in the same position as if the name had not been struck off` MEANS
    IF `a person has applied to the Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the application by any person, the Court may give directions and make orders" (a "may" gated by "On the application": split site (ii), answer JUST FALSE: fork F-S3)

-- (4) "An application to the Court for such directions or orders may be made any time within 3 years after the date of restoration of the name of the foreign company to the register."
-- src:24886 | (4) An application to the Court for such directions or orders may be
-- src:24887 | made any time within 3 years after the date of restoration of the name
-- src:24888 | of the foreign company to the register.
@ref s 377D(4) (src:24886-24888)
GIVEN `the day the name of the foreign company was restored to the register` IS A DATE
      `the day the application to the Court is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377D(4) the application to the Court for the directions or orders may be made` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the name of the foreign company was restored to the register` `the day the application to the Court is made` 3 Years
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be made any time within 3 years after the date of restoration" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); "within 3 years after" is counted as "not later than 3 years after": fork F-P1)
